{"type":"text","timestamp":1794534944818,"sessionID":"ses_e2d67e4d1ffe4lBa28HlX5551k","part":{"id":"prt_1d29e1f3a002VaT0f8eTIeTVLQ","sessionID":"ses_e2d67e4d1ffe4lBa28HlX5551k","messageID":"msg_1d29e0edd001abdzNWvkt3tObS","type":"text","text":"**T012 done.** Changed only `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/lanes/semantic-shadow.ts`.\n\nWhat changed:\n1. Imports `OllamaModelNotLoadedError`, `OllamaRequestTimeoutError` and `OllamaBackendUnreachableError` from the local Ollama adapter shim.\n2. Adds `promptEmbeddingDisabledReason(error)`, which maps model-not-loaded to `prompt_embedding_model_missing`, the deadline error and request timeout to `prompt_embedding_timeout`, any other unreachable error to `prompt_embedding_unreachable`, and everything else to `prompt_embedding_failed`.\n3. The catch now records that mapped reason for the current call. A call-scoped `preEmbedFailure` flag keeps the three reasons set before the embed (`database_absent`, `adapter_unavailable`, `dim_mismatch`) from being overwritten by the plain throw that follows them. I used a per-call flag rather than testing the stored reason, because a stale reason from an earlier call would otherwise mask a later transport failure.\n\nVerify 1, `rg -n \"prompt_embedding_(model_missing|timeout|unreachable)\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/lanes/semantic-shadow.ts` (exit 0, three lines):\n\n```\n124:    return 'prompt_embedding_model_missing';\n127:    return 'prompt_embedding_timeout';\n130:    return 'prompt_embedding_unreachable';\n```\n\nVerify 2, `npx vitest run tests/scorer` from `$ADV` (exit 0, 0 failed):\n\n```\n Test Files  37 passed (37)\n      Tests  348 passed | 2 skipped (350)\n```\n\nBaseline before the edit was the same, 37 files passed and 348 passed with 2 skipped. `npm --prefix $ADV run typecheck` also exits 0, which I ran to confirm the new imports resolve.\n\nTwo notes for the orchestrator. The `git diff` for this file also contains the deadline race from T007, which was already uncommitted in the working tree and is not mine. `npx vitest run tests/scorer` passes without the new failure modes being exercised yet, since the degrade test covering them is T019. Nothing was left undone and nothing is blocked on the operator.","time":{"start":1794534940474,"end":1794534944818}}}
